<title>GERMANY: Ford-Werke says H1 97 profit up, sales down.</title>
<headline>Ford-Werke says H1 97 profit up, sales down.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group profit				 80	vs 75</p>
<p>    Group sales				  13,900  vs 14,200</p>
<p>    Group vehicle sales (units)	    567,000 vs 608,000</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    --Germany				    195,000 vs 231,000</p>
<p>    --Export				     372,000 vs 377,000</p>
<p>    Group vehicle production		 508,000 vs 538,000</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    44,453  down 3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Forde-Werke AG, a unit of U.S. carmaker Ford Motor Co.</p>
<p>Ford-Werke said its German market share remained at 11.3 percent during the first half of the year but that its market share improved to 12.8 percent in June from 11.0 percent in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
